course: dictionary
lesson: 6712
title: Offend and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To offend someone is to make them upset, hurt or annoyed by what you say or do. «I don't mean to offend you» is a polite way of saying you are sorry if your words might hurt someone.
explain: Use the words around offend to work out its meaning. «No offence, but» warns you that the next words might upset someone. «In the UK people value queuing very highly, and jumping the queue makes them upset» shows why knowing customs helps you avoid offending anyone.
explain: Offend can also mean to be nasty to your senses: «The smell offended my nose.» In news or law language, to offend means to break a law, and an offender is a criminal. Alice says, «I wish the creatures wouldn't be so easily offended!», which means they get upset very quickly.
fact: Offend means to make someone upset, hurt or annoyed.
fact: The forms are offend, offends, offended and offending.
fact: «The smell offended my nose» means the smell was nasty or unpleasant.
fact: In formal or news language, to offend means to break a law or commit a crime.
fact: Useful phrases are «no offence» and «I don't mean to offend you».
exercise: The Mouse told Alice, «you're so easily offended.» What does offended mean? | Lost in a forest | Made of wood | Thrilled and full of joy | *Upset or hurt by something said
exercise: «The smell offended my nose.» Does offend mean nice or nasty here? | Loud and noisy | Hidden away | Nice and sweet | *Nasty and unpleasant
exercise: In news language, an offender is someone who does what? | Makes a delicious meal | Is always happy | *Breaks the law | Sings very well
test: Which phrase is a polite warning that your next words might upset someone? | Let's go outside | Pass the salt | Look at that cloud | *No offence, but
test: In news language, what does to offend mean? | To sing loudly | To make a cake | To feel tired | *To break a law or commit a crime
exam: Why does knowing customs such as queuing in the UK help you? | It helps you win every game | It helps you forget your manners | It helps you jump the queue faster | *It helps you avoid upsetting people
